EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Cradle_and_The_Crescent_TheSilkRoad_LesserSteppeSpirits" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Cradle & The Crescent - Lesser Steppe Spirits"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-07"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Cradle_and_The_Crescent_Core_Ext"

    # Lesser Steppe Spirits (Chapter Nine: The Silk Road & Beyond, p181): one being, its printed stat lines verbatim fields.

    #t69e10d8a9e9a8bc0ebaa8f ^"Lesser Steppe Spirits" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOmeyTfuLwkiC9FmXsz8PTO6 ^"Creature"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Location" LIST [#te7caee397b52bcc8711419 ^"Transoxiana and the East"]
            ^"Might Realm" STRING "Magic" FIXED
            ^"Magic Might" STRING "30-45 (Auram, Terram, or rarely Aquam or Herbam). All are considered genii loci of their particular steppe."
            ^"Typical Powers" STRING "Creator of Winds or Earth, Guide, Manifestation, Presence, Ruler of Winds or Earth. All Steppe Spirits possess the Ways of the Steppe Virtue and some have the ability to Grant Major Supernatural Virtues to their chosen messengers."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Cradle & The Crescent"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 181
        }
        DESCRIPTION "At its settled fringes, where the Great Steppe has begun to fray under the advance of settled communities, the Great Tengri has engendered lesser spirits at the cost of some of its own power. These lesser spirits are considered genii loci of a particular region, stretches of grassland that can range in size from a small valley, to the size of a large European kingdom. Three possible fates await such lesser fragment spirits.\n\n*Survival:* The genius locus of the local steppe is strong enough to hold its own against the encroachment of the mundanes and the Dominion. These spirits give rise to magical steppes, such as the southeast plains of Russia around the Sea of Azov, the Dzungarian depression, and the distant eastern plains of Mongolia. Between such peripheries, the Great Steppe spirit rules unchecked, only slightly diminished in power. Beyond these buffers, only lesser nature spirits and faeries are found.\n\n*Dissolution: *The genius locus of the steppe is too small to maintain its control over the steppe, or else it borders on more powerful areas that sap its strength until nothing remains. These spirits leave behind a mundane steppe. Examples include Pannonia, where the effects of the nearby Dominion of the Byzantine Empire have forced the lesser steppe spirits to flee into the deeper steppe. Likewise, the Hungarian plain, hemmed in by the arc of the Carpathians, where the formerly nomadic Magyars have settled, has also been sapped of its remaining strength, becoming an isolated promontory of Divine pasture.\n\n*Replacement: *The genius locus has dwindled and been replaced by another supernatural being. This most commonly gives rise to a Faerie steppe at the edges of settlement and pastoralists. The power of the original spirit is subsumed by a Faerie incarnation that feeds off the folktales told by the descendents of nomads. The towns along the Jaxartes border a Faerie steppe."
    }

}
